{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c42b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07750-3853-73c0-b383-0773367c2b50"},"sequence":112,"recorded_at":1780531400000219,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"875962f6-cab0-4746-ab6f-6a0b56e31c4c"},"task_id":"875962f6-cab0-4746-ab6f-6a0b56e31c4c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"875962f6-cab0-4746-ab6f-6a0b56e31c4c","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/open_member_windows.go`.\n1|package secprim\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"os\"\n5|\t\"path/filepath\"\n6|\t\"syscall\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// openCommitRelative is the Windows best effort for the guard commit\n10|// walk: Go has no openat, so each component is Lstat-checked against\n11|// the root-joined path before the final open. A symlink or reparse\n12|// point on the path returns the shared errCommitSymlink signal, which\n13|// the caller refuses as \"member symlink escape\".\n14|//\n15|// Stated bounds. The check-then-open race remains: a swap between the\n16|// component Lstat and the final open is not detected, and staging\n17|// roots being owner-only directories only narrows that window to the\n18|// owner. The walk additionally cannot see through the handle the way\n19|// the unix walk does: the root handle is validated as a directory by\n20|// the caller, but the component descent re-resolves the root path\n21|// string. Windows behavior in this package is compile-and-vet only,\n22|// never executed.\n23|//\n24|// Reparse coverage. The Lstat gate refuses ModeSymlink (true symlinks:\n25|// Go 1.23+ sets the bit only for IO_REPARSE_TAG_SYMLINK) and\n26|// ModeIrregular (every other reparse point — junctions, mount points,\n27|// AppExecLinks, cloud placeholders — which Go maps to ModeIrregular,\n28|// never to ModeSymlink). A junction-to-directory therefore refuses\n29|// here rather than passing the directory check the way a\n30|// symlink-only gate would admit it.\n31|func openCommitRelative(root *os.File, rootPath string, _ string, segments []string) (*os.File, error) {\n32|\t_ = root\n33|\tcurrent := rootPath\n34|\tfor _, segment := range segments[:len(segments)-1] {\n35|\t\tcurrent = filepath.Join(current, segment)\n36|\t\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(current)\n37|\t\tif err != nil {\n38|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n39|\t\t}\n40|\t\tif info.Mode()&(os.ModeSymlink|os.ModeIrregular) != 0 {\n41|\t\t\treturn nil, errCommitSymlink\n42|\t\t}\n43|\t\tif !info.IsDir() {\n44|\t\t\treturn nil, syscall.ENOTDIR\n45|\t\t}\n46|\t}\n47|\tfull := filepath.Join(rootPath, filepath.Join(segments...))\n48|\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(full)\n49|\tif err != nil {\n50|\t\treturn nil, err\n51|\t}\n52|\tif info.Mode()&(os.ModeSymlink|os.ModeIrregular) != 0 {\n53|\t\treturn nil, errCommitSymlink\n54|\t}\n55|\treturn os.OpenFile(full, os.O_RDONLY, 0)\n56|}\n57|\n58|// clearNonblock is inert on Windows: the Windows open sets no\n59|// non-blocking flag.\n60|func clearNonblock(_ *os.File) error {\n61|\treturn nil\n62|}"}}}
