{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c433","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07750-3853-73c0-b383-0773367c2b50"},"sequence":116,"recorded_at":1780531400000227,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f83ab188-f336-4a11-944a-ad1a5b9b1498"},"task_id":"f83ab188-f336-4a11-944a-ad1a5b9b1498","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f83ab188-f336-4a11-944a-ad1a5b9b1498","chunk":"Read text file `internal/secprim/open_member_unix.go`.\n1|//go:build !windows\n2|\n3|package secprim\n4|\n5|import (\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\n9|\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// openCommitRelative walks one validated member from the staging-root\n13|// directory handle to an open file descriptor without ever re-resolving\n14|// a path string: every component is opened relative to the previous\n15|// component's descriptor with openat. Intermediate components carry\n16|// O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY, so a symlinked directory on the path fails\n17|// with ELOOP instead of redirecting the walk outside the root; the\n18|// final component carries O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK, so a trailing symlink\n19|// fails with ELOOP and a FIFO returns immediately instead of stalling\n20|// the opener until a writer appears. Descriptors pin what they opened:\n21|// a rename or swap after any step cannot retarget a descriptor the\n22|// walk already holds, which is what closes the validate-then-open\n23|// TOCTOU rather than repeating it with more steps.\n24|//\n25|// The walk reports no refusal of its own: ELOOP maps to the shared\n26|// errCommitSymlink signal (refused as \"member symlink escape\" by the\n27|// caller) and every other failure returns raw (refused as \"open\n28|// failed\" with its cause). Shape checks on the final descriptor stay\n29|// with the caller, which stats the descriptor rather than the path.\n30|func openCommitRelative(root *os.File, _ string, member string, segments []string) (*os.File, error) {\n31|\tprevious := -1\n32|\tcurrent := int(root.Fd())\n33|\tfor _, segment := range segments[:len(segments)-1] {\n34|\t\tnext, err := unix.Openat(current, segment,\n35|\t\t\tunix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_NOFOLLOW|unix.O_DIRECTORY|unix.O_CLOEXEC, 0)\n36|\t\tif err != nil {\n37|\t\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n38|\t\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n39|\t\t\t}\n40|\t\t\treturn nil, classifyCommitErr(current, segment, err)\n41|\t\t}\n42|\t\tif previous >= 0 {\n43|\t\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n44|\t\t}\n45|\t\tprevious, current = next, next\n46|\t}\n47|\tlast := segments[len(segments)-1]\n48|\tfinal, err := unix.Openat(current, last,\n49|\t\tunix.O_RDONLY|unix.O_NOFOLLOW|unix.O_CLOEXEC|unix.O_NONBLOCK, 0)\n50|\tif previous >= 0 {\n51|\t\t_ = unix.Close(previous)\n52|\t}\n53|\tif err != nil {\n54|\t\treturn nil, classifyCommitErr(current, last, err)\n55|\t}\n56|\treturn os.NewFile(uintptr(final), member), nil\n57|}\n58|\n59|// classifyCommitErr sorts the walk failures: a symlink anywhere on the\n60|// path becomes the escape signal, while a missing component, a file\n61|// where a directory stands, or a permission failure stays raw for the\n62|// caller's open-failed refusal.\n63|//\n64|// The errno alone does not name the shape on every kernel: Linux\n65|// reports ELOOP for an O_NOFOLLOW openat meeting a symlink, while\n66|// Darwin reports ENOTDIR for the O_DIRECTORY half of the same event.\n67|// Either errno therefore re-examines the component with fstatat at\n68|// AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW — still relative to the parent descriptor, so\n69|// no path string is re-resolved — and only a component that is a\n70|// symlink right now becomes the escape signal. A swap between the\n71|// failed open and this check fails closed in every direction: each\n72|// outcome (symlink, directory, missing) refuses, and only the rule\n73|// name differs.\n74|func classifyCommitErr(parent int, segment string, err error) error {\n75|\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ELOOP) {\n76|\t\treturn errCommitSymlink\n77|\t}\n78|\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ENOTDIR) {\n79|\t\tvar status unix.Stat_t\n80|\t\tif fstatErr := unix.Fstatat(parent, segment, &status, unix.AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW); fstatErr == nil {\n81|\t\t\tif status.Mode&unix.S_IFMT == unix.S_IFLNK {\n82|\t\t\t\treturn errCommitSymlink\n83|\t\t\t}\n84|\t\t}\n85|\t}\n86|\treturn err\n87|}\n88|\n89|// clearNonblock drops O_NONBLOCK from an admitted regular file so a\n90|// borrowed descriptor never leaks the flag to its reader. Regular-file\n91|// reads ignore the flag either way.\n92|func clearNonblock(file *os.File) error {\n93|\treturn unix.SetNonblock(int(file.Fd()), false)\n94|}"}}}
