24 Prompt refusal text   KILLED TestPromptRefusalCarriesNeutralizedText\n73|  R28 Log                   KILLED TestTextEmissionNeutralizesHostileContent\n74|  R28b Prompt interactive   KILLED TestTextEmissionNeutralizesHostileContent\n75|provhost/runner.go:\n76|  R26  Env != nil -> len(Env) > 0        KILLED TestExecRunnerEmptyEnvIsDenyAll\n77|  R26b drop the Env wiring entirely      KILLED TestExecRunnerDeliversExactlyTheBuiltEnv + EmptyEnvIsDenyAll\n78|  R25n CheckArgv strips NUL first        KILLED TestExecRunnerRefusesUnusableExecutable\n79|        'Run(\"bad\\x00bin\") = *exec.Error ..., want *secprim.Error'\n80|  R25e gate applied only when executable == \"\"   KILLED (same test, same message)\n81|\n82|== G-E: denominator and survivors ==\n83|deriveRefusals over the candidate's non-test sources (12 files):\n84|  argv.go 5 | env.go 9 | nofollow.go 14 | path.go 13 | TOTAL 41 | STRAYS []\n85|  -> matches the reported 41 component by component.\n86|Narrowing mutants on the deletion-only env gates (all six killed by TestBuildEnvRefuses):\n87|  env value NUL, allowlist arm -> prefix-only          KILLED\n88|  env value NUL, literals arm  -> prefix-only          KILLED\n89|  env value encoding, allowlist arm -> len(value) > 4  KILLED\n90|  env value encoding, literals arm  -> len(value) > 4  KILLED\n91|  env allowlist duplicate -> len(name) > 3             KILLED\n92|  env literal collision   -> len(key) > 3              KILLED\n93|Survivor checks:\n94|  N7  drop ModeNamedPipe disjunct alone        SURVIVES  (bound correct: !mode.IsRegular() subsumes)\n95|  N24 drop the directory arm alone             KILLED    TestCheckRegularTarget + TestOpenNoFollowFile\n96|                                                          -> \"withdrawn as invalid\" is wrong\n97|  RV-S1 target symlink -> mode == ModeSymlink  KILLED    TestCheckRegularTarget\n98|  R12  withinRoot drop slash boundary          SURVIVES  (declared defensive)\n99|  RV-S2 withinRoot -> return true              SURVIVES  (same, stronger form)\n100|defensiveSites bound verified by relaxing the shared grammar\n101|(scalar.ParseRelativePath admits \"..\" segments):\n102|  grammar weakened, withinRoot intact  -> TestGuardPrefixCheckIsLoadBearing PASSES\n103|                                          (prefix conjunct catches the escape)\n104|  grammar weakened + withinRoot=true   -> FAILS: 'Resolve(\"x/../..\") escaped to \"/stage\"',\n105|                                          '24 admitted members escaped the root'\n106|  -> the defensive site and its rationale are both load-bearing as stated.\n107|\n108|== WINDOWS reparse mapping, checked against $GOROOT/src/os/types_windows.go (go1.25.5) ==\n109|(*fileStat).mode():\n110|  IO_REPARSE_TAG_SYMLINK            -> ModeSymlink       refused\n111|  default arm (junction/MOUNT_POINT, AppExecLink, cloud placeholder)\n112|                                    -> ModeIrregular     refused\n113|  IO_REPARSE_TAG_AF_UNIX            -> ModeSocket        passes Lstat gate, caught by CheckRegularTarget\n114|  IO_REPARSE_TAG_DEDUP              -> no type bit       admitted (Go's explicit \"close enough to regular\")\n115|modePreGo1_23() (GODEBUG=winsymlink=0): MOUNT_POINT -> ModeSymlink, still refused.\n116|=> escape-capable tags established; the \"every other reparse point\" universal has\n117|   two counterexamples, neither an escape. Advisory.\n118|\n119|== TREE INTEGRITY ==\n120|git read-tree HEAD; git add -A .; git write-tree\n121|  -> 703ee895c6b5f8bc2e6a97cb4aff7e538ce79c90  (before probes)\n122|  -> 703ee895c6b5f8bc2e6a97cb4aff7e538ce79c90  (after all reverts)\n123|All mutants restored from /tmp file backups; no repo-wide git restore/checkout used.\n124|No zz_*, .bak, or plant_* residue in the tree.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c723","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07750-3853-73c0-b383-0773367c2b50"},"sequence":492,"recorded_at":1780531400000979,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb"},"call_id":"call_01a07751098f7043ae04f6abc187ad72","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2ciy0s/TASK-260830-2ciy0s_secprim-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2ciy0s — safe path/argv/environment primitives (outcome, rev2)\n2|\n3|Round 2. Fixes all eight blocking findings of `TASK-260830-2ciy0s_review-verdict-rev1.md`\n4|(B1–B8), including the two live vulnerabilities (B1 containment escape, B2 FIFO hang).\n5|Work left UNCOMMITTED in the story worktree on top of trunk `157a54c`; no commits made.\n6|\n7|## What changed since rev1\n8|\n9|- `internal/secprim/nofollow.go` — `OpenNoFollowFile` clears `O_NONBLOCK` after\n10|  admission; new `Guard.Open(root, member)` commit entry: validation (member\n11|  grammar + managed set) and handle-relative commit in one entry point.\n12|- `internal/secprim/open_member_unix.go` (new) — `openat` walk with `O_NOFOLLOW`\n13|  per component, `ELOOP`/`ENOTDIR`-plus-`fstatat` escape classification, `O_NONBLOCK`\n14|  final open, `clearNonblock` hook.\n15|- `internal/secprim/open_member_windows.go` (new) — best-effort Lstat component\n16|  walk with the stated check-then-open bound; refuses `ModeIrregular` reparse\n17|  points, not just `ModeSymlink`.\n18|- `internal/secprim/open_nofollow_unix.go` — `O_NONBLOCK` on the file open.\n19|- `internal/secprim/open_nofollow_windows.go` — refuse `ModeIrregular` alongside\n20|  `ModeSymlink`, with the Go-runtime-source reparse mapping stated.\n21|- `internal/secprim/errors.go` — the single-construction-site rule now names the\n22|  full shape space (no aliases, literals, `new(Error)`, factories).\n23|- `internal/secprim/inventory_test.go` — derivation rewritten: alias fixpoint,\n24|  `Error`-literal / `new(Error)` / factory-call / factory-decl / value-escape\n25|  strays, plus `TestRefusalInventoryClosesBypassShapes` (control + 7 plants).\n26|- `internal/secprim/classes_test.go` — recursive emission scan (110 files,\n27|  fail-closed on parse errors); five `nopath` rows restated as archive-format\n28|  bounds; census vocabulary bound stated.\n29|- `internal/secprim/open_unix_test.go` (new, unix-only) — B1 escape fixture\n30|  (lexical `Resolve` admits, commit `Open` refuses), honest-member read,\n31|  six commit shapes, FIFO-through-opener with hang timeout.\n32|- `internal/secprim/render_test.go` — 16-rune corpus fed from the same slice it\n33|  asserts; per-rune rows for all previously unwitnessed code points.\n34|- `internal/secprim/path_test.go` — managed-set exactness (`A/B` refused),\n35|  empty-directory refusal, double-encoded overlong case, seam-driven\n36|  `Guard.Open` stat-failure arm.\n37|- `internal/secprim/redact_test.go` — compact-colon case (first-pass `:` arm's\n38|  unique shape).\n39|- `internal/cliresult/render_wiring_test.go` — success-`Emit`, `Progress`, and\n40|  `Prompt`-refusal hostile-content tests (all six text paths now driven).\n41|- `internal/provhost/runner_env_test.go` — `TestExecRunnerEmptyEnvIsDenyAll`\n42|  through `/usr/bin/env` (nil vs empty as distinct obligations).\n43|- `README.md` — claims corrected to the proven bounds (see below).\n44|\n45|## B1 — containment now composes (was: live escape)\n46|\n47|Vector: `NewGuard(stage)` + `stage/sub -> outside` symlink + `Resolve(\"sub/loot\")`\n48|returned `stage/sub/loot` and `OpenNoFollowFile` read `ESCAPED` outside the root.\n49|`O_NOFOLLOW` constrains only the final component; `Resolve` answers the lexical\n50|question only.\n51|\n52|Fix: `Guard.Open(root *os.File, member string)` validates (grammar + managed set)\n53|then walks `openat` per component from the `OpenNoFollowDir` handle with\n54|`O_NOFOLLOW` on every component — no path string is re-resolved. A symlinked\n55|intermediate fails the walk and refuses as `member symlink escape` (commit half\n56|of §16.3); a re-validated string is not used anywhere on this path. Darwin\n57|reports `ENOTDIR` (not `ELOOP`) for `O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY` meeting a symlink,\n58|so either errno re-examines the component with `fstatat(AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW)`,\n59|still descriptor-relative; any swap between the failed open and the check fails\n60|closed (every outcome refuses, only the rule name differs).\n61|\n62|Driven by: `TestGuardOpenRefusesSymlinkedParent` (pins `Resolve` admitting the\n63|lexical join AND `Open` refusing it), `TestGuardOpenAdmitsHonestMembers`,\n64|`TestGuardOpenRefusesCommitShapes` (final symlink, missing member/intermediate,\n65|unmanaged, grammar, nil/file root handles), N23/N24b/D12/D13 mutants below.\n66|\n67|## B2 — opener refuses FIFOs (was: hangs forever)\n68|\n69|`open(2)` read-only on a writer-less FIFO blocks in the kernel before the\n70|post-open shape check runs. Fix: `unix.O_NONBLOCK` on the unix file open and on\n71|the commit-walk final open; the post-open `CheckRegularTarget` refusal is now\n72|reachable, and admitted regular files are cleared of the flag.\n73|\n74|Driven by: `TestOpenNoFollowFileRefusesFifoWithoutBlocking` — drives the\n75|production opener in a goroutine with a 10 s timeout, so a regression fails\n76|instead of stalling the suite. `fifo_unix_test.go` still covers the pure\n77|predicate; the opener behavior is covered here.\n78|\n79|## B3 — all six cliresult sites driven (was: 3 of 6)\n80|\n81|`Log`, interactive `Prompt`, failure `Emit` were driven. Added:\n82|`TestTextSuccessEmissionNeutralizes` (success `Emit` → stdout, R27),\n83|`TestProgressEmissionNeutralizes` (TTY `Progress`, R23),\n84|`TestPromptRefusalCarriesNeutralizedText` (non-interactive refusal text with a\n85|hand-computed neutralized expectation, R24 — an unwired site fails the exact\n86|comparison rather than hiding behind `%q`). README now enumerates the six\n87|instead of claiming \"every text path\" uncovered.\n88|\n89|## B4 — nil vs empty allowlist (was: surviving R26)\n90|\n91|`TestExecRunnerEmptyEnvIsDenyAll` runs `/usr/bin/env` through\n92|`ExecRunner{Env: []string{}}` and requires a byte-empty child environment, so\n93|no helper marker travels in the environment under test. Together with\n94|`TestExecRunnerNilEnvInherits` the `!= nil` boundary is pinned from both sides:\n95|under the `len(Env) > 0` mutant the parent-only marker leaks and the test fails\n96|(N22). Unix execution check; skipped on Windows (compile-and-vet only there).\n97|\n98|## B5 — inventory gate closed over the shape space (was: 4 of 4 bypasses walked through)\n99|\n100|`deriveRefusals` replaces the identifier-keyed walk: constructor-alias fixpoint\n101|(`var`, `:=`, `=`, alias-of-alias), `Error` literals (direct and `secprim.`\n102|qualified) outside constructor bodies, `new(Error)`, calls to package `*Error`\n103|factories (functions and methods; `WithCause` is the one allowlisted decorator),\n104|factory declarations whose body never reaches a constructor, and constructor\n105|names escaping as values. Aliases resolve to their underlying constructor so\n106|exemptions keep working.\n107|\n108|Evidence, two layers. Committed: `TestRefusalInventoryClosesBypassShapes` feeds\n109|all eight shapes through the same `deriveRefusals` the audit uses — control\n110|(bare call, clean site), A (var alias), B (literal), C (method factory: decl +\n111|call + literal strays), D (local binding), E (value escape), F (`new(Error)`),\n112|G (alias of alias). Live (this run, reverted after, tree verified identical):\n113|control + reviewer plants A–D written as real production files, full suite run\n114|per plant — CONTROL caught (`never fired`), A caught (`alias`), B caught\n115|(`Error literal`), C caught (`factory`), D caught (`alias`).\n116|\n117|## B6 — corpus feeds all 16 (was: 10 fed, 16 asserted)\n118|\n119|`TestEscapeForTerminalOutputBytes` feeds the `forbidden` slice it asserts, so\n120|feed and assertion cannot drift again; per-rune table rows added for U+202A–\n121|U+202D, U+2068, U+2069, U+200E, U+061C, U+200C. R9b/R7/R7c now kill (N8/N9).\n122|\n123|## B7 — recursive scan, honest rows (was: one level, five overstated rows)\n124|\n125|`TestNoArchiveEmissionPath` walks all of `internal/` recursively (110 production\n126|files, up from the one-level scan), fails closed on unreadable/unparseable\n127|files, and names violating paths. Live probe this run: `archive/zip` planted in\n128|`internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen` is caught with its path (reverted after).\n129|The five `nopath` dispositions now claim exactly the proven bound (no\n130|archive-writer import anywhere under `internal/`, nested packages included —\n131|not the absence of every non-archive emission shape), and the Machine\n132|authentication row states the census vocabulary bound (13 tokens; names outside\n133|it are outside the witness).\n134|\n135|## B8 — denominator and honest mutant kinds (was: 6 of 35, deletions as narrowing)\n136|\n137|Derived refusal exits: **41** (argv 5, env 9, nofollow 14 = 8 rev1 + 6 new\n138|`Guard.Open` sites, path 13). Battery below: every row applied to the working\n139|tree and run as a standalone process in this session; the tree was verified\n140|byte-identical after (sha256 manifest over all touched files; only expected\n141|delta is the compact-colon test added before the manifest… correction: the\n142|manifest was recorded before the compact-colon insert, so that one file differs\n143|by exactly that insert — confirmed by inspection; no `.mutbak`/`zz_*` residue).\n144|\n145|### Narrowing — 27 applied, 27 killed (killed/applied = 27/27)\n146|\n147|| Mutant | Admits exactly | Named failing test |\n148||---|---|---|\n149|| N1 drop `%25`-unwrap on encoded-dot arm | doubly-encoded dots | TestCheckMemberPathRefuses/double-encoded_dot |\n150|| N2 drop `%25`-unwrap on overlong arm | doubly-encoded overlong separators | TestCheckMemberPathRefuses/double-encoded_overlong |\n151|| N3 ADS `:` → `::` | single-colon streams | .../windows_ads(+nested) |\n152|| N4 drop trailing-space disjunct | trailing-space segments | .../windows_trailing_space |\n153|| N5 segment loop `[:1]` | non-first-segment violations | .../windows_lpt |\n154|| N6 managed lookup `ToLower` | case variants of managed members | TestGuardManagedSet |\n155|| N7b drop NamedPipe disjunct + irregular catch-all (two-arm) | FIFOs | TestCheckRegularTarget |\n156|| N8 bidi lower `0x202a`→`0x202b` | U+202A | TestEscapeForTerminalOutputBytes |\n157|| N9 isolate upper `0x2069`→`0x2068` | U+2069 | TestEscapeForTerminalOutputBytes |\n158|| N10 C1 upper `0x9f`→`0x9e` | U+009F | TestEscapeForTerminalOutputBytes |\n159|| N11 C0 `<0x20`→`<0x1f` | U+001F | TestEscapeForTerminalOutputBytes |\n160|| N12 argv NUL first-element-only | NUL past argv[0] | .../nul_argument |\n161|| N13 argv encoding first-element-only | invalid UTF-8 past argv[0] | .../invalid_utf8 |\n162|| N14 argv empty first-element-only | empty past argv[0] | .../empty_element |\n163|| N15 env name length 128→129 | 129-rune names | TestIsEnvName |\n164|| N16 env name leading digit | 9LIVES | TestIsEnvName |\n165|| N17 minSecretRunes 8→9 | 8-rune secrets | TestRedactCorpusValues |\n166|| N18 PEM suffix widened (WIDENING) | non-private BEGIN blocks | TestRedactPrivateKeyBlocks |\n167|| N19 success-Emit wire identity (R27) | raw stdout | TestTextSuccessEmissionNeutralizes |\n168|| N20 Progress wire identity (R23) | raw progress | TestProgressEmissionNeutralizes |\n169|| N21 Prompt-refusal wire identity (R24) | raw refusal text | TestPromptRefusalCarriesNeutralizedText |\n170|| N22 runner Env `!=nil`→`len>0` (R26) | empty allowlist inherits | TestExecRunnerEmptyEnvIsDenyAll |\n171|| N23 ELOOP-only escape classification | Darwin misreport as open-failed | TestGuardOpenRefusesSymlinkedParent |\n172|| N24b drop directory arm + catch-all (two-arm) | directories | TestCheckRegularTarget |\n173|| N25 argv `len==0`→`len<0` | empty vectors | .../empty_vector |\n174|| N26 first-pass sep `\"=\"` only | compact colon pairs | .../compact_colon |\n175|| N27 drop DEL from control case | DEL | .../del |\n176|\n177|### Deletion (existence probes) — 15 applied, 15 killed\n178|\n179|D1 duplicate-allowlist arm → duplicate_allowed; D2 literal-collision arm →\n180|literal_collides; D3 one scrubber-table entry → TestSensitiveKeyListIsReviewed;\n181|D5 managed-set arm → TestGuardManagedSet; D6 encoded-dot arm → encoded_dot;\n182|D10 Log-only wire → hostile-content test; D11 runner.Env ignored → built-env\n183|test; D12 final O_NOFOLLOW flag → final_symlink; D13 intermediate O_NOFOLLOW\n184|flag → symlinked-parent test; D14b argv gate retirado (narrow re-application\n185|keeping the import) → TestExecRunnerRefusesUnusableExecutable with\n186|`Run(\"\") = *errors.errorString exec: no command, want *secprim.Error`;\n187|D15 userinfo arm → TestRedactURLUserinfo; D16 corpus arm →\n188|TestRedactCorpusValues; D17 nil-stat arm → seam test (killed via panic);\n189|D18 guard-root delegation → TestGuardResolve; D19 kernel-open-error ignore →\n190|TestOpenNoFollowFile (killed via panic).\n191|\n192|### Instrument probes — 2 applied, 2 killed; bypass probe — 1 applied, 1 killed\n193|\n194|D8 census token drop → TestSecretSiteRosterIsComplete (orphans); D9 class-row\n195|rename → TestExclusionClassRosterIsComplete (orphans); D7 token-preserving\n196|shell (`\"s\"+\"h\"` + `os/exec`, no literal token) → TestPackageLaunchesNoProcess\n197|(behavioral half).\n198|\n199|### Survivors with stated bounds — 2\n200|\n201|- N7 (drop NamedPipe disjunct only): SURVIVES — the `!mode.IsRegular()`\n202|  catch-all subsum\n203|...[truncated 5836 chars]","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
