{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07750-3853-73c0-b383-0773367c2b50"},"sequence":581,"recorded_at":1780531400001157,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"35bc7cf0-58fd-477b-bed8-e6904a52ec83"},"task_id":"35bc7cf0-58fd-477b-bed8-e6904a52ec83","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"35bc7cf0-58fd-477b-bed8-e6904a52ec83","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-18-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"secprim\\\\|Guard.Open\\\\|symlink\\\\|O_NOFOLLOW\\\\|inventory\\\\|reparse\\\\|ModeIrregular\\\" README.md 2>&1 | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"Find secprim README section\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"51:`CLAUDE.md` is a relative symlink to that canonical file.\\n120:inventory of a bound section from it. The embedded document never reaches the\\n238:derive the production refusal-site inventory from source and fail when a new\\n244:inventory test and each names the check that covers it. An omitted\\n286:The two seams take deliberately different symlink stances, and both are pinned\\n288:resolves symlinks and then applies the Section 3.2 value kind to the resolved\\n289:target: a configuration file symlinked onto a regular file loads, a root\\n290:symlinked onto a directory loads, and either link pointed at the wrong kind\\n293:resolves symlinks before comparison where it speaks about them at all, so\\n294:refusing an ordinary dotfiles or Application Support symlink would be an\\n295:invented constraint; a dangling configuration symlink accordingly resolves to a\\n297:without creating anything. The durable migration seam does not follow symlinks,\\n418:The package derives its refusal inventory from its own source: every refusal\\n492:The package derives its refusal inventory from its own source: every\\n506:arm, so a planted arm or a deleted branch reddens in either direction. This inventory is independent of the per-package refusal inventories in [`internal/provider`](internal/provider) above and [`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) below (see [Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate](#specification-to-code-ownership-gate)): each package derives its own refusal arms from its own source in its own test file, and the three share no inventory code or table.\\n513:[`internal/secprim`](internal/secprim) implements the shared safe\\n540:does not contain: a symlinked intermediate directory redirects any\\n541:path-string open outside the root, because `O_NOFOLLOW` constrains only\\n542:the final component. The commit half is `Guard.Open`, which walks every\\n544:`O_NOFOLLOW` per component on unix, never re-resolving a path string)\\n545:and refuses a symlinked parent at commit time as `member symlink\\n547:trailing symlink (`O_NOFOLLOW` on unix; an Lstat gate refusing symlinks\\n548:and irregular reparse points with a stated check-then-open TOCTOU bound\\n576:of every non-archive emission shape). The refusal inventory derives all\\n580:the Lstat reparse mapping is established from the Go runtime source\\n581:(`ModeSymlink` only for true symlinks, every other reparse point\\n582:surfacing as `ModeIrregular`, which the gate also refuses). The package\\n589:go test ./internal/secprim -count=1\\n590:go test ./internal/secprim -cover -count=1\\n762:symlink rules, and recursive submodule state/depth/count constraints that can\\n808:The per-member inventory is checked against the production `requireExactMembers`\\n814:previously carried whole member sets outside the inventory. The scanned file set\\n822:fixture inventory also derives every required nested-object path and proves that\\n828:ancestor is a declared `file`, `symlink` or `hardlink` is rejected, reusing the\\n830:path's ancestor set, so a symlink or file parent cannot carry children into\\n871:UTF-8 bytes, including Blob media type, Manifest symlink target, workspace\\n874:Every declared range bound is proven at both of its limits, and the inventory\\n975:derived from production the same way the bounds inventory is: every\\n1150:it the union of every other pinned vocabulary. The pinned inventory kills a\\n1185:rule — are already pinned by the derived coupling inventory and the clause\\n1194:existing coupling inventory, which owns that clause. A seventh mutant, skipping\\n1210:submodule state, sparse-pair drift, and hardlink/symlink/count violations\\n1309:symlink, or not a directory at all are each refused with the immutable digest\\n1330:which is not a symlink, belongs to the effective user and already carries\\n1343:The schema and its indexes come from one closed inventory.\\n1397:The unfiltered localstore package run derives the projection refusal inventory\\n1416:inventory can only prove the first. A fixture that also trips an earlier check\\n1420:is not a symlink, is owned by the effective user, and already carries owner-only\\n1439:`kind` and `name` are subsumed by the inventory key lookup, and the\\n1657:The measured inventory is 18 of 44 registered command tags, 2 of 4 registered\\n1940:### Refusal guard inventory\\n1991:STATED BOUND of the inventory itself: the derivation is exhaustive over\\n2095:the immutable v0.5.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\\n2116:clause of that inventory, quote it verbatim beginning on the exact `SPEC.md`\\n2198:AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\\n2201:named test, which the inventory resolves textually),\\n2280:inventory (`census_test.go`) requires every production refusal arm\\n2293:Successful output reports ownership inventory counts and the measured coverage\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4804,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1201,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
