{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d691","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07750-3853-73c0-b383-0773367c2b50"},"sequence":2467,"recorded_at":1780531400004929,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"fc69ac0e-9867-43a1-9121-d6d02d6c39df"},"task_id":"fc69ac0e-9867-43a1-9121-d6d02d6c39df","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"fc69ac0e-9867-43a1-9121-d6d02d6c39df","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-88-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 30 LOGBOOK.md; echo ...; grep -c \\\"\\\" LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head before appending\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 1553 — Shared-environment boundary round-2 rework: admit hole closed by delegation, shape census, 27-mutant battery\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-3bkz0c round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev3, B1/B2/F1/F2 blocking + B2b). Freeze on sessadapter/dirnode production lifted for exactly this fix. Production: sessadapter/dirnode decodeStrictObject delegate frame verdicts to environ.DecodeStrictObject (fault translation only); buggy hasLoneSurrogateEscape/readUTF16Escape copies deleted; environ.rawUint53 hardened with trailing-data check; dead environ.validCapability deleted. Tests: frame corpus proves both directions (3 composed rows added, 7 verdicts flipped with absent-phrase pins), shape census (25 rows) + 14 synthetic controls + grammar fresh-name rule + delegation pin, environ unit tests for uint53/sorted-strings-halves/Fault rendering, both leaves' arm censuses derive the bridge from environ source.\\n- FINDING (B2): witness `\\\\\\\\ud800\\\\udc00` (escaped backslash + literal ud800 + real lone low) admitted by sessadapter.DecodeTuple (Version rewritten to `\\\\\\\\ud800`+U+FFFD) and dirnode.CheckScanRequest while environ/canonicaljson/provhost refused — the raw scan misread quoted text as a high surrogate and paired it with the following real escape. Closed by delegation, not by widening the scan. All five judges refuse post-fix (probe logs kept).\\n- FINDING (corpus one-sidedness): frameCorpus sampled backslash-run parity but never an even run WITH a following real escape — green over the hole. The corpus now proves both directions: run-parity rows (over-strict side, verdicts flipped to member arms with frame phrase absent) plus even-run-plus-real-escape compositions (admit-hole side).\\n- FINDING (B1): live-planted all 7 reviewer shapes into internal/provider — old name census caught 2/7 (ledgered-name func/method); new name+shape census catches 7/7 plus a fresh-name grammar copy (evidence log kept). Shape census also surfaced 5 canonicaljson rune measures and scalar's third-spelling raw-scan gate that the name census never saw; scalar/provhost/canonicaljson copies ledgered as unification residue in TASK-260906-33xcnc.\\n- FINDING (F1/F2): environ had zero production callers and 6 functions at 0%; now DecodeStrictObject/HasLoneSurrogateEscape are called from both facades, coverage 76.1%→89.8%, no function at 0%. Denominator re-derived from production: 31 refuse arms + 58 boolean exits = 89. Battery: 27 applied / 27 killed (26 narrowing + token-preserving T1 with census green and 7 behavioral rows reddening); 22 of 89 exits directly killed, 67 residue stated by function.\\n- FINDING (new, fixed): environ.rawUint53 admitted `12a` as 12 (Decoder reads one value and stops); covered by new M4 mutant + trailing check. Sibling sessadapter/dirnode/provhost copies share the texture but are unreachable via production paths (frame gates first) — tracked in TASK-260906-33xcnc, not fixed here.\\n- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-3bkz0c_round2.md (5-judge witness table, 7/7 live-plant proof, 27-row mutant table, residue table, AC mapping) + updated TASK-260830-3bkz0c_boundary.md. Follow-up TASK-260906-33xcnc created and referenced.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1 -p 2` exit 0 (19 pkgs), environ `-race` exit 0, cover 89.8%, `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet` (3 pkgs) exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (94 cases, unchanged), `go build ./...` exit 0.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1347 — Shared-environment boundary leaf: one library plus fail-closed agreement battery\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-3bkz0c (third/final leaf of STORY-260830-3drr2m). New package `internal/environ` (decode.go, tuple.go, observation.go, doc.go): single strict-frame decoder with string-walk surrogate semantics, rune measure, env-id/SemVer/arch grammars, exact six-member Tuple, §10.8.1 Environment Observation reusing the tuple model. Battery: census, frame/measure/tuple/identity agreement, observation. Frozen `sessadapter`/`dirnode` production untouched. Commit afdba1d (signed), PR #35 published.\\n- FINDING: sessadapter+dirnode raw-scan surrogate gates REFUSE wire bodies carrying literal backslash-u text (`cursor` value `\\\\ud800` text) while environ+provhost+canonicaljson string-walk gates ACCEPT — proven via DecodeTuple/CheckScanRequest/Canonicalize. sessadapter `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON` is one-directional (`!localRefuses && sharedRefuses`) and hides exactly this class. Ledgered in frame_agreement_test.go; unifying the frozen scanners is the recorded follow-up.\\n- FINDING: truncated/malformed escapes refuse at the surrogate arm (raw scan) vs the syntax arm (string walk); wrong identity schema/version refuses at the member arm (provhost) vs the dispatch registry (canonicaljson). Same verdicts, different arms — ledgered per-judge, not papered over.\\n- FINDING: battery caught its author's parity error — run-3 backslashes (`\\\\\\\\\\\\ud800`) are a real lone escape (odd runs escape, even runs quote), not divergence; row corrected to all-refuse before green.\\n- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-3bkz0c_boundary.md (7/7 AC rows with call sites) + TASK-260830-3bkz0c_mutation-log.md. Narrowing mutants 6/6 killed (N1/N2/N3/N4/N6 + token-preserving T1 raw-scan rewrite with census still green); D1 delete-only killed, scored as existence only. Tree sha-verified identical post-battery.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (19 pkgs), environ `-race` exit 0, cover 76.1%, `go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (unchanged), catalog generate no-diff, `go build ./...` exit 0.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off with CR published (review/landing are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n...\\n1003\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6532,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1633,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
