{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7e9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07750-3853-73c0-b383-0773367c2b50"},"sequence":2639,"recorded_at":1780531400005273,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"54033564-b97c-4244-a825-33fd926ad5cb"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round 3 is ready for review (handed off to review, status `to-review`, checklist 18/18).\n\nWhat closed each finding:\n\n- **C1** — `Guard.Open` now binds the handle to `guard.root` via `guardRootMatches` (fstat dev/ino through `os.SameFile`) before descending, refusing foreign handles as `guard root mismatch` from shared code so both platforms answer identically. `TestGuardOpenRefusesForeignRootHandle` (cross-platform) plus a matched-handle control; with the check removed the test reads `FOREIGN` bytes.\n- **C2** — classify-before-close at both walk sites; `TestGuardOpenRefusesDeepSymlinkedParent` pins full `member symlink escape` strings at 3 and 4 segments. Reverting one site reproduces the reported `open failed: ... not a directory` exactly.\n- **C3** — reviewer's preferred option: the identifier-spelling bound is stated in `errors.go`, the derivation comment, and the README, pinned by `TestRefusalInventorySpellingBoundIsStated`. Live H/I/J bypass green, CONTROL caught, token-preserving shell probe caught.\n- **C4** — evidence attached as 5 file resources (18,836-byte outcome doc intact, verified byte-complete in the board store). N24 restored as the arm-drop spelling (kills); the `Size() > 0` spelling was run and survives as vacuous — documented, uncounted. Scripted D14 is a compile-fail, superseded by the killing D14b.\n\nEvidence: 31/31 AC rows driven with call sites, 22/29 rules narrowing-covered, battery 59 killed of 61 applied (N7 survives with bound), denominator at 42 sites, R12 double probe, Windows escape-capable set with the two counterexamples. All gates exit 0 (full suite/cover, race, vet, Windows vet/build, gofmt, tracecheck); tree OID `7cae2bfa` identical across battery, plants, and probes. Work left uncommitted in the story worktree.","reason":null}}
